# etude-ldf mirror namespace verification

The pre-land audit found and corrected one contradictory classification: the
rejected nested `refs/etude/remotes/...` layout could fail the general safety
contract yet still receive `OK fetch-mirror`. The legacy destination is now an
explicit FAIL and only the landed sibling `refs/etude-mirror/...` layout counts
as mirror coverage.

Verified:

- `TestDoctorRejectsNestedRemoteMirrorLayout` passes and requires a non-zero
  result, `FAIL fetch-refspec`, `WARN fetch-mirror`, and no contradictory OK.
- `TestDoctorPinsLandedSiblingMirrorNamespace` passes and independently pins
  the production mirror prefix to `refs/etude-mirror/origin/runs/`.
- The correction adds no write or network command and does not change the local
  mirror comparison model.
